@CLS@@X0CManage Caller Log

@X0E@X0D<@X0ED@X0D>@X0E  DELETE CALLER LOG - Deletes log for current node.
     WARNING - ONCE DELETED PCBOARD CANNOT RECOVER THAT LOG!

@X0E@X0D<@X0EP@X0D>@X0E  PRINT CALLER LOG - The log will be displayed as well as sent to the
     printer defined in PCBsetup.

@X0D<@X0ES@X0D>@X0E  SEARCH CALLER LOG FOR TEXT - Provides search capabilities to locate any
     text within the caller log.  Simple one word or phrase searches, or
     boolean searches using AND, OR, and NOT operators. Case is ignored.

@X0D<@X0EV@X0D>@X0E  VIEW CALLER LOG - This permits viewing of the caller log.  The most
     current caller is displayed first.

Regular searches for system erros is a good idea and can be accomplished
by typing 1 S FAIL | ERROR on the command line.
@X07
